<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36114" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoēbē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φοίβη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The moongoddess</i>, <i>sister of
				Phœbus</i>, i. e. <i>Diana</i>, <i>Luna</i>, or <i>the moon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vento semper rubet aurea Phoebe,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 431</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. A. 3, 371</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 18</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoebe venantibus assit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 3, 2, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jaculatrix Phoebe,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					H. 20, 229</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">innupta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					1, 476</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 7, 366</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>night</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tertia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					6, 235</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A daughter of Leda and sister of Helen</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 8,
			77</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Daughter of Leucippus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 1,
				679</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 1, 2, 15</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
